hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21071","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Muhammad, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were washing his daughter, peace be upon her, and he said: wash her three times, or five, or more than that if you see fit, with water and lote leaves, and put in the last camphor or something of camphor. When you finish, inform me. She said: when we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: shroud her in it. He said: and Hafsah said: he said: wash her an odd number, three or five or seven. He said: and Umm Atiyyah said: we braided her hair into three braids."
"21072","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took from us at the pledge was that we not wail. None of us fulfilled it except five women."
"21073","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seven raids, staying behind them in their dwellings, making food for them, attending to their sick, and treating their wounded."
"21074","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid informed us, Hisham informed us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by my father and mother, commanded us to bring out the young unmarried women and those of seclusion and menstruating women on the day of Fitr and the day of sacrifice. As for menstruating women, they keep away from the prayer place and witness good and the supplication of the Muslims. He said: it was said: what about one of them who has no outer garment? He said: then let her sister dress her from her outer garment."
"21075","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid informed us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah, she said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Yazid said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: a woman does not mourn beyond three except for a husband, for she mourns over him four months and ten days. And she does not wear a dyed garment except Asb, and she does not apply kohl, nor touch perfume, except at her purification. Yazid said: or in her purification, when she is purified from her menstruation, a bit of Qust and Azfar."
"21076","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: when Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: wash her an odd number, three or five, and put in the fifth camphor or something of camphor. When you wash her, inform me. She said: then we informed him, and he gave us his waist-wrapper and said: shroud her in it."
"21077","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: when this verse was revealed: they pledge to you that they will not associate anything with Allah, up to His saying: nor disobey you in what is right, she said: among it was wailing. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, except the family of so-and-so, for they had helped me in the pre-Islamic period, so I must help them. She said: then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: except the family of so-and-so."
"21078","Abu Said narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Uthman al-Kilabi Abu Yaqub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Atiyyah al-Ansari narrated to us, from his grandmother Umm Atiyyah, she said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he gathered the women of the Ansar in a house, then he sent Umar ibn al-Khattab to them, may Allah be pleased with him. He stood at the door and greeted, and they returned the greeting. He said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you. We said: welcome to the Messenger of Allah and the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. And he said: you pledge that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor commit adultery, nor kill your children, nor bring slander you fabricate between your hands and your feet, nor disobey him in what is right. We said: yes. Then we extended our hands from inside the house, and he extended his hand from outside the house. Then he said: O Allah, bear witness. And he commanded us with the two Eids to bring out the freed and menstruating women, and he forbade following funerals, and there is no Friday upon us. And I asked her about His saying: nor disobey you in what is right, she said: we were forbidden from wailing."
"21079","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Abu Zayd Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hisham, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: I was among those who pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Among what he took from us was that we not wail, nor speak privately with men except a close relative."
"21080","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Umm Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah, she said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to bring out the young unmarried women and menstruating women and those of seclusion. As for menstruating women, they keep away from the prayer place and witness good and the supplication with the Muslims."
"21081","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Ibn Sirin took his washing from Umm Atiyyah, she said: we washed the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded us to wash her with lote three times, if it cleanses, otherwise five, if it cleanses, otherwise more than that. She said: then we saw that more than that is seven."
"21082","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: I was informed that Umm Atiyyah said: one of the daughters of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, and he commanded us to wash her three or five or more than that if you see fit, and to put in the last washing something of lote and camphor."
